A new GitHub REST API version is available: <%= @latest_version %>

Hi <%= @user.display_login %>,

A new version of the GitHub REST API, <%= @latest_version %>, is now available.

We recommend updating to the latest version by sending the header `X-GitHub-Api-Version: <%= @latest_version %>` with every request. You can learn more and find migration guidance in the API versioning documentation:
<%= @changelog_url %>

<% if @deprecating_versions.present? -%>
The previous API versions will be retired on the following dates:

<% @deprecating_versions.each do |version, deprecation_date| -%>
- <%= version %> — retires on <%= deprecation_date %>
<% end -%>

<% end -%>
If you've already upgraded to <%= @latest_version %> then please disregard this email.

Thank you,
The GitHub API Team

